{
  "1 call site/A source location where a function is called, not a website.": "1 sito di chiamata",
  "{0} call sites/Source locations where a function is called, not websites.": "{0} siti di chiamata",
  "1 function/Counts the functions a body was copied into by inlining.": "1 funzione",
  "{0} functions/Counts the functions a body was copied into by inlining.": "{0} funzioni",
  "1 instr/Abbreviation of \"machine instruction\".Keep the abbreviation short - it sits in a one-line CodeLens.": "1 ist.",
  "{0} instr/Abbreviation of \"machine instructions\".Keep the abbreviation short - it sits in a one-line CodeLens.": "{0} ist.",
  "1 spill/Register allocation term: a value the compiler had to write out to the stack because no CPU register was free.Use the established term in your language, not \"spill\" as in a spilled liquid.": "1 scarico",
  "{0} spills/Register allocation term: values the compiler had to write out to the stack because no CPU register was free.Use the established term in your language, not \"spill\" as in a spilled liquid.": "{0} scarichi",
  "1 reload/Register allocation term: reading a spilled value back from the stack into a CPU register.The counterpart of \"spill\".": "1 ricaricamento",
  "{0} reloads/Register allocation term: reading spilled values back from the stack into CPU registers.The counterpart of \"spill\".": "{0} ricaricamenti",
  "Instructions/Machine/IR instructions in the called function that the optimizer could not fold away.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Istruzioni",
  "Calls inside callee/Cost charged for the calls the called function itself makes.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Chiamate nel chiamato",
  "Switch lowering/Cost of turning a switch statement into jump tables and comparison chains.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Riduzione dello switch",
  "Argument setup/Cost of preparing the arguments passed to a call.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Preparazione degli argomenti",
  "Indirect calls/Cost charged for calls through a function pointer, whose target is not known.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Chiamate indirette",
  "Cold calling convention/Cost charged because the called function uses the calling convention for rarely executed code.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Convenzione di chiamata fredda",
  "Relative loads/Cost of loads made through a relative offset, as used by virtual call tables.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Caricamenti relativi",
  "Stack promotion savings/A saving, shown as a negative number: inlining would let the optimizer keep a stack variable in registers.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Risparmi per promozione nello stack",
  "Eliminated loads/A saving, shown as a negative number: inlining would remove loads from memory.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Caricamenti eliminati",
  "Call overhead removed/A saving, shown as a negative number: inlining removes the cost of performing the call itself.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Overhead della chiamata rimosso",
  "~{0} instructions/An approximate instruction count derived from an inline cost. Keep the leading ~ (about).": "~{0} istruzioni",
  "Includes the last-call-to-static bonus: the function is deleted after inlining./Explains a very large saving: this was the only remaining call to a function private to the file.": "Include il bonus dell'ultima chiamata a funzione statica: la funzione viene eliminata dopo l'inlining.",
  "(weight {0}, threshold {1})/Follows \"inlined\" or \"not inlined - too costly\". {0} is the inline weight LLVM computed for the call (can be negative) and {1} the budget it had to stay under.Both are plain integers with no unit.": "(peso {0}, soglia {1})",
  "{0}: {1}/One cost contributor: {0} is its label, e.g. \"Switch lowering\", {1} a plain integer.": "{0}: {1}",
  "{0}: {1} ({2})/The instruction contributor: {0} is its label, {1} a plain integer, {2} a reading such as \"~338 instructions\".": "{0}: {1} ({2})",
  "+{0} more/Ends a truncated list of cost contributors. {0} is how many were left out.": "+{0} altri",
  "Missed reduction: {0} (argument address escapes)/{0} is a weight reduction the optimizer could not take because the address of an argument was used, so the value could not be kept in registers.A plain integer with no unit.": "Riduzione mancata: {0} (l'indirizzo dell'argomento sfugge)",
  "{0}, {1}/Joins two entries of a comma-separated list.": "{0}, {1}",
